==================================================
2. GENERAL ENVIRONMENT / CLIMATE
==================================================

Create a semi-arid environment.

The map should NOT be:
- completely desert
- completely green
- snowy
- tropical

Instead use a natural mixture of:

- dry soil
- light brown earth
- beige terrain
- rocky ground
- sparse dry grass
- occasional green patches
- small natural elevation changes
- hills
- rocky ridges

The terrain should have visual variation but remain believable as one connected environment.

==================================================
3. TERRAIN HEIGHT
==================================================

The terrain must NOT be completely flat.

Create subtle natural elevation variation across the map:

- gentle hills
- shallow valleys
- small slopes
- rocky elevated areas
- natural depressions
- occasional larger hills

IMPORTANT:
Do not create extreme mountains throughout the interior.

Most of the interior must remain suitable for future:
- cities
- military bases
- airport
- Red Zone
- roads
- Metro entrances
- combat areas

We will decide the exact locations of those later.

==================================================
4. OUTER MAP EDGE
==================================================

Around the ENTIRE outer edge of the Homs-shaped map, create natural geographical barriers.

Use:

- low mountains
- rocky hills
- cliffs where appropriate
- elevated terrain
- rock formations

These should visually communicate:

"THIS IS THE END OF THE PLAYABLE MAP."

Do NOT create a giant artificial wall.

Do NOT create visible invisible-wall-style structures.

The edge should look like natural geography.

The mountains around the perimeter should generally be moderate rather than enormous.

They should discourage the player from leaving while still looking realistic.

